---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import Header from '../components/Header.astro'
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro'
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | Ringlume"
  description="How Ringlume collects, processes, stores, and protects data used for automated call-handling, including call records, voice transcripts, and contact information."
>
  <Header />

  <main class="scrim min-h-screen pt-24 pb-20">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <h1 class="text-h1 font-bold text-fg-1 mb-4">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="text-fg-3 mb-12">Last Updated: August 8, 2026</p>

      <div class="glass glass-fill glass-regular glass-card max-w-none space-y-10 rounded-[32px] p-6 sm:p-10 lg:p-14">

        <!-- 1. Introduction -->
        <section>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-fg-1 mb-4">1. Introduction</h2>
          <p class="text-fg-2 leading-relaxed">
            Ringlume ("Company," "we," "us," or "our") is committed to protecting your
            privacy. This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, disclose, store, and
            safeguard your personal information and data when you use our virtual receptionist and
            automated call-handling and voice-processing technology, plus all related software,
            platforms, and communication tools
            (collectively, the "Services").
          </p>
          <p class="text-fg-2 leading-relaxed mt-4">
            By using the Services, you consent to the collection and processing of your data as
            described in this Privacy Policy. If you do not agree with our data practices, please
            discontinue use of the Services immediately.
          </p>
        </section>

        <!-- 2. Information We Collect -->
        <section>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-fg-1 mb-4">2. Information We Collect</h2>
          <p class="text-fg-2 leading-relaxed">
            We collect various categories of information to provide and improve our Services:
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-fg-1 mt-6 mb-3">2.1 Information You Provide Directly</h3>
          <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-fg-2 space-y-2 ml-4">
            <li>Information provided for service setup or support, such as your name, email address, business name, and phone number</li>
            <li>Billing and payment information processed through our payment provider, such as billing address and transaction details. Ringlume does not receive your full card number.</li>
            <li>Business documents uploaded to set up the service with information about your business</li>
            <li>Communications sent to us via email, WhatsApp, or other channels</li>
          </ul>

          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-fg-1 mt-6 mb-3">2.2 Information Collected Automatically</h3>
          <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-fg-2 space-y-2 ml-4">
            <li>Website usage data (pages visited, time spent, click patterns, device information)</li>
            <li>IP addresses and approximate geolocation data</li>
            <li>Browser type, operating system, and device identifiers</li>
            <li>Cookies and similar tracking technologies</li>
          </ul>

          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-fg-1 mt-6 mb-3">2.3 Call and Voice Data</h3>
          <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-fg-2 space-y-2 ml-4">
            <li>Telephone call recordings (both inbound and outbound)</li>
            <li>Complete voice transcripts and conversation logs</li>
            <li>Caller identification information (phone numbers, caller ID data)</li>
            <li>Call metadata (duration, timestamps, call outcome, transfer status)</li>
            <li>Sentiment analysis results and emotional context indicators</li>
            <li>Appointment and scheduling data extracted from calls</li>
          </ul>

          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-fg-1 mt-6 mb-3">2.4 Third-Party Integration Data</h3>
          <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-fg-2 space-y-2 ml-4">
            <li>Customer records synchronized through connected integrations</li>
            <li>Contact information imported from third-party platforms</li>
            <li>Calendar and scheduling data from connected calendar services</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <!-- 3. How We Use Your Data -->
        <section>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-fg-1 mb-4">3. How We Use Your Data</h2>
          <p class="text-fg-2 leading-relaxed">
            We use the information we collect for the following purposes:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-fg-2 space-y-2 mt-4 ml-4">
            <li><strong class="text-fg-1">Service Delivery:</strong> To provide, operate, maintain, and improve the virtual receptionist and related automated call-handling services</li>
            <li><strong class="text-fg-1">Service Setup & Improvement:</strong> To set up how the service handles calls using your business-specific data and improve response accuracy and conversation quality</li>
            <li><strong class="text-fg-1">Call Processing:</strong> To record, transcribe, analyze, and store telephone communications processed through the Services</li>
            <li><strong class="text-fg-1">Appointment Management:</strong> To schedule, confirm, and manage appointments based on caller interactions</li>
            <li><strong class="text-fg-1">Reporting & Analytics:</strong> To generate post-call reports, performance analytics, and business reports</li>
            <li><strong class="text-fg-1">Automated Follow-up Actions:</strong> To trigger SMS confirmations, email notifications, customer-record updates, and follow-up sequences</li>
            <li><strong class="text-fg-1">Customer Support:</strong> To respond to inquiries, troubleshoot issues, and provide technical assistance</li>
            <li><strong class="text-fg-1">Legal Compliance:</strong> To comply with applicable laws, regulations, and legal processes</li>
            <li><strong class="text-fg-1">Security:</strong> To detect, prevent, and address fraud, unauthorized access, and other malicious activity</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <!-- 4. Data Storage & Security -->
        <section>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-fg-1 mb-4">4. Data Storage & Security</h2>
          <p class="text-fg-2 leading-relaxed">
            We implement enterprise-grade security measures to protect your data, including:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-fg-2 space-y-2 mt-4 ml-4">
            <li><strong class="text-fg-1">Encryption:</strong> All data is encrypted in transit using TLS 1.3 and at rest using AES-256 encryption standards</li>
            <li><strong class="text-fg-1">Secure Infrastructure:</strong> Data is stored on SOC 2 Type II-compliant cloud infrastructure with redundant backups</li>
            <li><strong class="text-fg-1">Access Controls:</strong> Strict role-based access controls ensure only authorized personnel can access sensitive data</li>
            <li><strong class="text-fg-1">Regular Audits:</strong> We conduct regular security assessments and penetration testing to identify and address vulnerabilities</li>
            <li><strong class="text-fg-1">Incident Response:</strong> We maintain a comprehensive incident response plan to address any security breaches promptly</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="text-fg-2 leading-relaxed mt-4">
            While we implement robust security measures, no method of electronic transmission or
            storage is 100% secure. We cannot guarantee absolute security but will promptly notify
            affected users in the event of a data breach as required by applicable law.
          </p>
        </section>

        <!-- 5. Call Recording & Transcription -->
        <section>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-fg-1 mb-4">5. Call Recording & Transcription Policy</h2>
          <p class="text-fg-2 leading-relaxed">
            Our automated call-handling and voice-processing service records and transcribes
            telephone conversations for the following purposes:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-fg-2 space-y-2 mt-4 ml-4">
            <li>Quality checks and ongoing improvement of response accuracy</li>
            <li>Training data used to improve how the service understands callers and generates responses</li>
            <li>Compliance documentation and dispute resolution</li>
            <li>Business analytics and performance reporting</li>
            <li>Automated follow-up actions after calls (SMS confirmations, customer-record updates, etc.)</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="text-fg-2 leading-relaxed mt-4">
            Call recordings and their associated transcripts are stored securely and are accessible
            exclusively through the Client dashboard. Recordings are retained for the duration of
            the active subscription and for a period of ninety (90) days following subscription
            termination, after which they are permanently deleted unless retention is required by
            applicable law.
          </p>
          <p class="text-fg-2 leading-relaxed mt-4">
            <strong class="text-fg-1">Important:</strong> The Client is solely responsible for
            ensuring compliance with all applicable federal, state, and local call recording consent
            laws in their jurisdiction. Ringlume provides tools that automatically tell callers when
            a call may be recorded but assumes no liability for the Client's compliance with recording
            consent requirements.
          </p>
        </section>

        <!-- 6. Data Sharing & Third Parties -->
        <section>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-fg-1 mb-4">6. Data Sharing & Third Parties</h2>
          <p class="text-fg-2 leading-relaxed">
            We do not sell, rent, or trade your personal information to third parties for their
            marketing purposes. We may share your data in the following limited circumstances:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-fg-2 space-y-2 mt-4 ml-4">
            <li><strong class="text-fg-1">Service Providers:</strong> With trusted third-party vendors who assist in operating our Services, including cloud hosting, telecommunications providers, and our payment provider for payment processing and billing, bound by applicable data processing obligations</li>
            <li><strong class="text-fg-1">Legal Requirements:</strong> When required by law, subpoena, court order, or governmental regulation</li>
            <li><strong class="text-fg-1">Business Transfers:</strong> In connection with a merger, acquisition, or sale of assets, with prior notice to affected users</li>
            <li><strong class="text-fg-1">With Your Consent:</strong> When you explicitly authorize data sharing with specific third parties through the platform settings</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <!-- 7. Your Rights -->
        <section>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-fg-1 mb-4">7. Your Data Rights</h2>
          <p class="text-fg-2 leading-relaxed">
            Depending on your jurisdiction, you may have the following rights regarding your personal
            data:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-fg-2 space-y-2 mt-4 ml-4">
            <li><strong class="text-fg-1">Access:</strong> Request a copy of all personal data we hold about you</li>
            <li><strong class="text-fg-1">Correction:</strong> Request correction of inaccurate or incomplete data</li>
            <li><strong class="text-fg-1">Deletion:</strong> Request deletion of your personal data, subject to legal retention requirements</li>
            <li><strong class="text-fg-1">Portability:</strong> Request a machine-readable copy of your data for transfer to another service</li>
            <li><strong class="text-fg-1">Restriction:</strong> Request restriction of processing in certain circumstances</li>
            <li><strong class="text-fg-1">Objection:</strong> Object to processing based on legitimate interests</li>
            <li><strong class="text-fg-1">Withdraw Consent:</strong> Withdraw previously given consent at any time</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="text-fg-2 leading-relaxed mt-4">
            To exercise any of these rights, please contact us at support@ringlume.com. We
            will respond to your request within thirty (30) days.
          </p>
        </section>

        <!-- 8. Data Retention -->
        <section>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-fg-1 mb-4">8. Data Retention</h2>
          <p class="text-fg-2 leading-relaxed">
            We retain your data for as long as necessary to provide the Services and fulfill the
            purposes described in this Privacy Policy:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-fg-2 space-y-2 mt-4 ml-4">
            <li><strong class="text-fg-1">Customer and Service Data:</strong> Retained for the duration of the active subscription plus 90 days</li>
            <li><strong class="text-fg-1">Call Recordings & Transcripts:</strong> Retained for the duration of the active subscription plus 90 days</li>
            <li><strong class="text-fg-1">Payment Records:</strong> Our payment provider retains payment records, and Ringlume retains billing records it receives, for seven (7) years where required by tax and financial regulations</li>
            <li><strong class="text-fg-1">Analytics Data:</strong> Aggregated and anonymized data may be retained indefinitely for service improvement</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <!-- 9. Cookies -->
        <section>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-fg-1 mb-4">9. Cookies & Tracking Technologies</h2>
          <p class="text-fg-2 leading-relaxed">
            Our website and third-party payment or billing tools may use cookies and similar
            tracking technologies to support functionality and enhance your experience:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-fg-2 space-y-2 mt-4 ml-4">
            <li><strong class="text-fg-1">Essential Cookies:</strong> Required for basic website functionality and security</li>
            <li><strong class="text-fg-1">Analytics Cookies:</strong> Help us understand how visitors interact with our website</li>
            <li><strong class="text-fg-1">Preference Cookies:</strong> Remember your settings and preferences</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="text-fg-2 leading-relaxed mt-4">
            You can control cookie preferences through your browser settings. Disabling essential
            cookies may affect website functionality.
          </p>
        </section>

        <!-- 10. Children's Privacy -->
        <section>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-fg-1 mb-4">10. Children's Privacy</h2>
          <p class="text-fg-2 leading-relaxed">
            Our Services are not directed to individuals under the age of 18. We do not knowingly
            collect personal information from children. If you become aware that a child has provided
            us with personal information, please contact us immediately, and we will take steps to
            delete such information.
          </p>
        </section>

        <!-- 11. Changes to This Policy -->
        <section>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-fg-1 mb-4">11. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
          <p class="text-fg-2 leading-relaxed">
            We reserve the right to update or modify this Privacy Policy at any time. Changes will
            be effective immediately upon posting on this page with an updated revision date. We
            encourage you to review this Privacy Policy periodically. Your continued use of the
            Services after any changes constitutes acceptance of the updated Privacy Policy.
          </p>
        </section>

        <!-- 12. Contact Us -->
        <section>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-fg-1 mb-4">12. Contact Us</h2>
          <p class="text-fg-2 leading-relaxed">
            If you have any questions, concerns, or requests regarding this Privacy Policy or our
            data practices, please contact us:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-none text-fg-2 space-y-2 mt-4">
            <li><strong class="text-fg-1">Email:</strong> support@ringlume.com</li>
            <li><strong class="text-fg-1">WhatsApp:</strong> +8801951284128</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

      </div>
    </div>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
